<!--
    calltargettype (GH-869): the target of an indirect call takes the
    function-pointer type the call states.

    Stage: P5 type recovery, after every variable has its final type and just
    before casts are decided. P0 assertion: option calltargettype on|off.

    Source, built twice: gcc 11 -O1 at 0x100000 and clang 14 -O2 at 0x100100
    (clang's symbols prefixed c_), both -fno-pic -fcf-protection=none, with the
    tables tbl at 0x200000, tbl2 at 0x200100, ctab at 0x200200 and ftab at
    0x200300, and a one-byte qsort stub at 0x100300:

        typedef void (*fp)(void);
        typedef int (*fp2)(int, long);
        typedef int (*cmpf)(const void *, const void *);
        typedef float (*f1)(float);
        struct ops { int (*op)(int); void *d; };
        extern fp tbl[];
        extern fp2 tbl2[];
        extern cmpf ctab[];
        extern f1 ftab[];
        int r1(int a, long b) { return a + (int)b; }
        void call(unsigned i) { tbl[i](); }
        int call2(unsigned i, int x) { return tbl2[i](x, 7) + 1; }
        int calls(struct ops *o, int v) { return o->op(v) * 2; }
        long twice(long (**t)(), long a)
        { long (*f)() = t[0]; return f(a) + f(a, a); }
        int chosen(int c, int x)
        { int (*f)(int, long) = c ? r1 : tbl2[0]; return f(x, 1) + f(x, 2); }
        int sorter(int *a, unsigned long n, unsigned w)
        { cmpf c = ctab[w];
          if (c(a, a + 1) > 0) qsort(a, n, sizeof *a, c); return a[0]; }
        void fstore(unsigned i, float *p) { p[0] = ftab[i & 1](p[1]); }

    Pass 1 (ctypes on, option calltargettype off, the shipped catalog default)
    is the bug: the prototype-less code pointer every target is typed as prints
    void *, so call, call2 and calls each call a void * (asserts 1, 3), which no
    C compiler accepts. Pass 2 (ctypes on, calltargettype on, what the
    aggressive preset selects) types each target from its call: the table entry
    is loaded through void (**)(void) (assert 2), the local holding a table
    entry is declared int (*)(unsigned int,unsigned long) and loaded through a
    pointer to it (asserts 4, 5), and the field read through an integer pointer
    is cast to int (*)(unsigned int) where it was cast to void * (asserts 6 to
    8). The cast count does not change.

    Every pass leaves these locals void * (asserts 9 to 16): twice calls one
    local with one and with two arguments; chosen's local receives the address
    of r1, whose own prototype C would have to match; sorter hands its local to
    qsort, whose comparator slot has the header's own type. Pass 2 casts the
    local at each of those calls to the call's own type instead (asserts 20 to
    23). fstore passes the float it loaded, which recovery holds as an unsigned
    int in xmm0. A type built from that unsigned int would pass it in edi and
    read the result from eax, so that call keeps void * in every pass rather
    than compile to one that computes something else.

    Pass 3 (ctypes off, calltargettype on) prints the upstream spelling it
    always printed: the option needs C's own spelling, so it does nothing there
    (asserts 17 to 19). Every assertion holds for the gcc and the clang build.

    Assertions span the combined output of the three passes.
-->
